            <ArticleTitle>Leveraging psychiatric and medical genetics to understand comorbid depression and obesity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>61-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1192/bjp.bp.116.194662</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Precision medicine in psychiatry is on the rise, and depression and obesity - two highly prevalent, comorbid and well-characterised phenotypes - are optimal targets for the approach. Add the bedrock susceptibility gene, FTO, and Riviera et al have identified a constellation of factors that could enhance clinical treatment of both disorders.</AbstractText>
